<header><p class="st-kicker">other · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Unitarian League</h1><p class="st-meta">1830 CE – 1831 CE · capital Córdoba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An alliance of nine Argentine interior provinces under General José María Paz, defeated by the federalists in 1831.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the civil wars between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unitarian-party">Unitarians</a>, who wanted a centralised <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentina</a>, and Federalists, General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-paz">José María Paz</a> took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 1829. He defeated the federal caudillo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-facundo-quiroga">Juan Facundo Quiroga</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-la-tablada">La Tablada</a> in 1829 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-oncativo">Oncativo</a> in 1830, and in 1830 the interior provinces formed the League of the Interior with Paz as Supreme Military Chief.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league joined nine provinces, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, Tucumán, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salta">Salta</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mendoza-argentina">Mendoza</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-juan-province-argentina">San Juan</a>, under Unitarian governors installed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-paz">Paz</a>'s backing. It was mainly a military alliance. In response, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-fe-argentina">Santa Fe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entre-rios-province">Entre Ríos</a> signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-pact">Federal Pact</a> in January 1831.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In May 1831 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-paz">Paz</a> was captured when soldiers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estanislao-lopez">Estanislao López</a> brought down his horse with boleadoras. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-facundo-quiroga">Quiroga</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unitarian-party">Unitarians</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-la-ciudadela">La Ciudadela</a> near Tucumán in November 1831, and the provinces joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-pact">Federal Pact</a>, forming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argentine-confederation">Argentine Confederation</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/unitarian-league.jpg" alt="Unitarian League" width="320" height="290"><figcaption>Image: KaasterMDK · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argentina_en_Enero_de_1831,_durante_la_Tercera_Guerra_Civil_Argentina.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1830 CE – 1831 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Córdoba</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>José María Paz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/argentina">Argentina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>League of the Interior, Liga del Interior</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1830&amp;focus=unitarian-league" aria-label="Unitarian League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3023 3322 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Unitarian League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3343 3578L3440 3589"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3440 3589h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3343 3578h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3343 3578h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Córdoba. <a href="/atlas?year=1830&amp;focus=unitarian-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

